meta {
  name: hub port check
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/fleet/port-check
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  port: 7700
}

docs {
  Whether a hub port is free on loopback right now: {port, free, thisHub}. free is false when the port cannot be bound or another program answers on 127.0.0.1 or [::1]; thisHub is true when this server's own hub holds it. 400 with reason (under-1024, app-range, server-port, not-a-port) and message for a port the hub may not take, refused before any bind. The fleet settings ask this before they save a port.
  
  Fence: host. Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
